{"id":"word:hebrew:H5057","type":"word","title":"נָגִיד","subtitle":"H5057 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a commander (as occupying the front ), civil, military or religious; generally (abstractly, plural), honorable themes","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to נָגִיד (H5057) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 44 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"נָגִיד (nâgîyd) means a commander (as occupying the front ), civil, military or religious; generally (abstractly, plural), honorable themes First listed occurrence: 1Chr 5 2."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"נָגִיד","transliteration":"nâgîyd","pronunciation":"naw-gheed'","strong":"H5057","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5057","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["נָגִ֔יד","נָגִ֖יד","לְ/נָגִיד֙","לְ/נָגִ֖יד","נְגִ֥יד"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",19],["HR/Ncmsa",8],["HNcmsc",6],["HNcmpa",4],["HTd/Ncmsa",3],["HC/R/Ncmsa",1],["HC/Ncmsa",1],["HNcmpc",1],["HR/Ncmsc",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"a commander (as occupying the front ), civil, military or religious; generally (abstractly, plural), honorable themes","usage":"captain, chief, excellent thing, (chief) governor, leader, noble, prince, (chief) ruler.","full":"H5057. nagid נָגִיד noun masculine leader (literally probably one in front ), ruler, prince; — absolute ׳נ 1Sam 9:16 31t.; construct נְגִיד (נְגִד) 2Kin 20:5-6 t.; plural נְגִידִים Job 29:10 3 t.; נְגִידֵי 2Chr 35:8 ; — ruler, prince Psalm 76:13; Prov 28:16 ; Job 29:10 ; 31:37 (in simile). Especially 1 of king of Israel: of Saul לְנ ׳מָשַׁח עַל (+ accusative of person), 1Sam 9:16 (subject prophet), compare of Solomon, subject people, 1Chr 29:22 ; 10:1 (subject ׳י ); of David לְנ ׳צִוָּהוּ עַל 1Sam 13:14 ; 25:30 , ׳נ צִוָּהוּ עַל 2Sam 6:21 (in these ׳י subject), לנ ׳היה על 5:2 , נ ׳היה על 7:8 ; 1Chr 11:2 ; 17:7 ; compare also 5:2 ; 2Chr 6:5 ; of David also נ ׳נָתַן ׳לְ Isa 55:4 ; of Solomon נ ׳לִהְיוֺת על אֹתוֺ צִוָּה 1Kin 1:35 ( ׳י subject); of Jeroboam נ ׳נתן על ( + accusative of person) 14:7 ( ׳י subject); so 16:2 of Baasha; of Hezekiah ׳נְ עַָמִּי 2Kin 20:5 ; ׳לְנ בְּאֶחָיו הֶעֱמִיד ( + accusative of person) 2Chr 11:22 (of Abijah, subject Rehob.); of Judah 1Chr 28:4 . 2 of a foreign ruler or prince Ezek 28:2 ; Dan 9:25-26 ,. 3 the title of some high official connected with the temple Jer 20:1 (of Pashhur) י ׳בבית נָגִיד פָקִיד וְהוּא and he was prince-overseer in, etc. (for ׳פ see 29:26 ); hence ׳נ האלהים בית 1Chr 9:11 ; 2Chr 31:13 ; 35:8 (three ב ׳נגידי ׳ה , including the high-priest), Neh 11:11 ; of high-priest Dan 11:22 נ ׳בְּרִית . 4 ruler in other capacities (late): of tribe 1Chr 27:16 ; 2Chr 19:11 ; of Korahites 9:20 ; of Aaronite warriors 2 Chron 12:27; of division of army 1Chr 13:1 ; 27:4 ; 2Chr 11:11 (commandant of fortress), 32:21 (in Assyrian army: || שַׂר ); of temple-treasuries 1Chr 26:24 , compare 2Chr 31:12 ; ׳נ הבית 28:7 (i.e. of palace?). 5 princely thimgs , plural abstract Prov 8:6 .","rootNote":"or נָגִד ; from 5046 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 5 2","keyReferences":["1Chr 5 2","1Chr 9 11","1Chr 9 20","1Chr 11 2","1Chr 12 28","1Chr 13 1","1Chr 17 7","1Chr 26 24"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":44,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 5 2","book":"1Chr","chapter":5,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/לְ/נָגִ֖יד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/R/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 9 11","book":"1Chr","chapter":9,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נְגִ֖יד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 9 20","book":"1Chr","chapter":9,"verse":20,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נָגִ֨יד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 11 2","book":"1Chr","chapter":11,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נָגִ֔יד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 12 28","book":"1Chr","c